# Historical findings, each verified not to be a credential.
#
# The working tree is clean — both values were replaced. These fingerprints
# refer to commits already pushed, and rewriting 25 commits of history over two
# non-secrets would cost more than it buys.
#
# 1. docs/aws-account-changes.md — an AWS KMS *key ID*.
#    Not a credential. Using a KMS key requires IAM permission; the ID alone
#    grants nothing, and it appears in every CloudTrail entry that touches the
#    key. It was still removed from the working tree, because it is an
#    account-specific identifier that made the document wrong for anyone else.
#
# 2. scripts/expired-credential-test.sh — a deliberately invalid JWT.
#    The test exists to prove that a rejected credential surfaces as
#    Unauthorized rather than as an empty cluster (ADR-0019), so it needs a
#    token the API server refuses. It was JWT-shaped, which made every scanner
#    flag it; it is now plainly not a token and still gets the 401.
#
# Anything new must be fixed, not added here.
